### Corrupt Python Package Handling

The code automatically checks the health of the shared Conda environment using `pip check` before installing new dependencies.
If corrupted, missing, or inconsistent Python packages are detected, it automatically force-reinstalls the dependencies defined in 
the project’s `requirements.txt` files and validates the environment again. This reduces manual intervention and helps prevent random pipeline 
failures caused by package corruption in the shared environment; if the automatic repair does not resolve the problem, the pipeline fails with
a clear error so the issue can be investigated.


###Jenkins Utility Jobs Guide

The Jenkins Utility Jobs Guide documents the shared self-service automation jobs available to project teams,
including what each job does, its required parameters, and how to use it. It also provides guidance for
teams that want to contribute new utility jobs and identifies where to get support.
